    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. Dealing with all those different legal backgrounds and potential fraud sounds like it would have been a nightmare for the merchants. Was there anything else that contributed to that sense of chaos or difficulty in managing the trade routes? Like, were there any specific social or environmental factors that made it harder for people to trust one another or follow those new commercial codes?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
