      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The vast environmental extremes and political fragmentation of the steppe created a transactional environment where trust was often lower and risk management was critical, leading merchants to rely increasingly on shared commercial codes rather than individual legal recourse. Environmental uncertainties, such as harsh winters and sandstorms, necessitated communal safety protocols that inadvertently reinforced the need for collective trust among married units or guilds, yet political betrayals by passing sultanates frequently undermined these fragile agreements. This constant interplay of ecological unpredictability and geopolitical volatility made the enforcement of international standards the primary defense mechanism for sustained long-distance commerce.",
